      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture of the code. Let me write the improved, more understandable version of the test.\n\nKey improvements I'll make:\n- Remove all unused helper methods, constants, and imports (dead code that clutters the class)\n- Extract magic numbers into named constants with clear meaning\n- Add explanatory comments for the loop mechanics (why `i * 2`, what `i * 2 + 4` means)\n- Use local named variables to clarify intermediate values in the assertionNow let me compile-check the generated test.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored file removes all unused helper methods, constants, and imports, and makes the test logic clearer through named constants (`HEX_CHARS_PER_BYTE`, `WINDOW_SIZE_IN_HEX_CHARS`, `NUM_SLIDING_WINDOWS`), descriptive local variables (`windowStart`, `windowEnd`, `decodedWindow`, `expectedWindow`), and explanatory comments that clarify the sliding-window mechanics."
    }
